Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:59:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Phase II: monodisperse dust IC + constant-kernel analytic
 gate (b1)

Adds the analytic validation for Rung 1 coagulation and the IC it needs.

dust_ic = 'monodisperse' (dust_grid.f90 / get_grain_radii dispatch): all grains
in bin 1, normalised to sum_k n_k m_k = initial_dtg_mass_ratio * AMU; empty bins
get a huge GTODN so their abundance is ~0. This is the single-size initial state
the closed-form Smoluchowski solution assumes.

tests/coag_gate.sh: permanent gate. Runs the dust-only fixture with the
monodisperse IC and constant kernel K0, sized so the trajectory spans the knee,
and asserts
  * gate (a): mass Sum m_k n_k conserved to machine precision;
  * gate (b1): total number N(t) = N0/(1 + K0*nH*N0*(t-t0)/2) within 5%.
Measured on the 16-bin fixture (N/N0 -> 0.098 over 2000 yr):
  gate (a) mass rel-err  = 5.4e-15
  gate (b1) decay rel-err= 2.2e-05   (at the DLSODES rtol=1e-4 floor)
Top-bin occupancy stays ~1e-26 over the window, so the Rung 1 overflow-skip
policy drops no flux and the boundary-free analytic solution is valid here.

Bug fix (input_output write_parameters): the coagulation settings were read but
never written back, so init's parameters.in rewrite silently dropped them and a
re-run would lose coagulation. Now coagulation / coagulation_kernel /
constant_kernel_k0 are persisted. Simulation numerics unchanged: coagulation-OFF
jac_weight_check is still identical (13450 entries, worst reldiff 1.8006e-3, 0
weight bugs).

Rung 1 (pure grain coagulation, constant kernel) is now validated end to end:
mass-exact and matching the analytic decay. Remaining follow-ups: wire the
dropped-flux diagnostic into the output stream; Brownian kernel (Rung 1b).
